course: dictionary
lesson: 8088
title: A remedy is a fix
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A remedy is something that cures an illness or helps you feel better, usually a medicine or treatment. A remedy can also be a way to fix a problem. «Natural does not mean safe: some herbal remedies can harm, or interact with other medicines.» The words «Natural does not mean safe» are the clue. They warn you that a remedy can still be dangerous, even when it comes from a plant.
explain: Some words tell you what a remedy does. «Medieval remedies such as herbs, bleeding and sweet flowers mostly did not work.» The word mostly and the words did not work tell you that people in the past used remedies that were not always helpful. Ask yourself: what does the sentence say about how well the remedies worked?
explain: Remedy can also be a verb, which means to put right or fix something. In formal writing, you might read «remedy the situation». Try swapping in fix: if the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: A remedy is a medicine or treatment that cures or helps an illness.
fact: «Natural does not mean safe»: some herbal remedies can harm people or interact with other medicines.
fact: Medicines can interact, making each other stronger or weaker, so doctors and pharmacists need to know about every remedy a person takes.
fact: Tu Youyou won the 2015 Nobel Prize for artemisinin, a malaria drug from a plant called sweet wormwood.
fact: «Quarantine» comes from the Italian word for forty, because some towns kept travellers apart for forty days.
exercise: «Medieval remedies such as herbs, bleeding and sweet flowers mostly did not work.» What does remedies mean here? | *Treatments for illness | Long, old stories | Holidays by the sea | Kinds of flower
exercise: «Natural does not mean safe: some herbal remedies can harm.» What does this sentence warn us? | Natural things are always better for you | Medicines never mix with anything | Herbal remedies are always safe | *Some herbal remedies can harm you
exercise: «Please remedy the situation.» What does remedy mean? | Make it worse | Ignore it completely | *Put it right or fix it | Start a new game
test: «Some medicines interact, making each other stronger or weaker, so doctors need to know about every medicine and herbal remedy a person takes.» Why do doctors need to know about every remedy? | Because remedies always taste sweet | Because doctors like long lists | *Because one medicine can change how another works | Because remedies are only for animals
test: Which of these is a home remedy? | A new pair of football boots | Ice cream on the beach | A bicycle with a bell | *Honey for a sore throat or cough
exam: Why does the sentence «Natural does not mean safe» matter when someone chooses a remedy? | Because remedies always taste nice | *Because some natural remedies can harm you or mix badly with medicines | Because natural things are always cheaper | Because you should only take remedies at night
